[SSF 130](/standarder/ssf-130) covers the design and installation of intruder and hold-up alarms in **alarm classes 1–4**. The required design and installation depend on the alarm class specified by the customer or insurer.

## Alarm classes

- Alarm class 1 applies where basic alarm monitoring is required.
- Alarm class 2 includes perimeter protection supplemented by interior volumetric detection.
- Alarm class 3 sets higher requirements for monitoring and tamper protection.
- Alarm class 4 covers rooms that may be excluded at lower classes.

## How SSF 200 differs

[SSF 200](/standarder/ssf-200) covers **physical burglary protection of buildings and premises**, using protection classes 1–3. It does not cover the design or installation of alarm systems. Protection class and alarm class are separate requirements that may apply together.

Always consult the current standard and the terms applicable to the particular site.
